this is my picture of the week Berlin's  landmark the Brandenburg Gate is  illuminated in the blood-red of the  Turkish flag following the attack on  Istanbul on New Year's Eve this  projection epitomizes the sense of  solidarity felt in Germany for turkey  two countries which have been linked  with each other for a very long time  we've seen the Brandenburg Gate light up  in different colors in the past year  France Belgium this seems like yet  another episode in some kind of mccobb  installation but this time it is  different whether you like it or not the  turkish kebab belongs to germany as much  as sour crab does there is a deep bond  between Germans and Turks a friendship  one that defies eight and violence and  that's what this picture is all about  millions of Turks are firmly rooted in  this society their pain is Germany's  pain these people they came here with  nothing but hope for a better life I  know them well my family is one of them  most jerks who traveled to Germany may  well have found what they were looking  for but they've also had to stay behind  watching from a distance as this long  string of attacks has devastated Turkey  this flag illuminating the Brandenburg  Gate the Turkish flag was deliberately  designed to look this way the red  symbolizes the blood of those who have  to give their lives in defense of the  Republic when will this flag finally be  read enough  [Music]
 

